<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:controls="clr-namespace:KinesisEdit.Controls">
  <!--
    The one icon that moves.

    Everything else about an icon is settled by Controls/Icon.cs (the 1.5px square-capped pen, the
    16px grid, the uniform fit) and by the call site, which names the geometry and the token brush
    it is painted with. There is deliberately no base `Icon` style here: an icon has no default
    colour in this design, and inventing one would hide the fact that a call site forgot to name a
    role.
  -->

  <!--
    Device art shares one authoring box.

    Themes/DeviceArt.axaml draws every board in the same 92x56 box - "boards are centred in it and
    drawn at true proportion relative to each other" - which is a fact about the art, not about any
    one call site, so it is stated once here. Fitting each silhouette's own ink instead would scale
    every device to the same extent and throw away exactly the relative proportion the drawings
    encode: a pedal would end up as wide as a contoured board.

    `Size` stays with the call site, because the same drawing is used at two sizes: 92 renders the
    art frame at 1:1 for a dashboard card, ~33 gives the silhouette in the empty-state picker. The
    fit is uniform, so 92x56 in a Size-square box letterboxes to Size x (Size * 56/92).
  -->
  <Style Selector="controls|Icon.deviceArt">
    <Setter Property="SourceBox" Value="0,0,92,56" />
  </Style>

  <!--
    The busy spinner: three quarters of a 14px ring, rotating once every 1.1s, linearly, forever
    (docs/design/handoff.md - "spinner = 14px circle, 1.5px stroke, one transparent quadrant, 1.1s
    linear spin").

    It lives in the style layer rather than in the control so the motion stays where the motion
    budget can see it, and so a spinner is one class at the call site:

      <controls:Icon Classes="spinner" Stroke="{DynamicResource AccentBrush}" />

    Four things this style settles, in order:

    1. `Data`. The mark is `IconScanning` (Themes/Icons.axaml) and nothing else, so the class name
       and the geometry are bound together in one place instead of at every call site.
    2. `SourceBox`. `IconScanning` is the one mark NOT authored on the 16px grid - it is drawn in a
       14x14 box centred on (7,7), because the spinner's size token is 14. The box has to be stated
       or the control would fit it as if it were a 16 box, shrink the ring and park its centre a
       pixel off the control's, and the rotation would wobble. The 14 here is `SpinnerSize` by
       construction; a Rect cannot be composed out of a resource, so it is written out and guarded
       by a test rather than bound.
    3. The rotation itself: `RenderTransformOrigin` at the control's centre, which is where the
       fitted geometry's centre lands, and a linear 0-360 loop.
    4. The duration is written out rather than bound. Themes/Motion.axaml records it as
       `DurationSpinnerRotation`, but an `Animation` is not part of the logical tree, so a
       `DynamicResource` on it would resolve to nothing and silently give a zero-length loop. This
       is the same rule the recording pulse follows (Styles/Keyboard.axaml).

    It keeps spinning under reduce-motion, deliberately. The spinner is not decoration: it is the
    only affordance saying the app is still working, and a frozen one reads as a hung app - a worse
    outcome for the very user reduce-motion exists to protect. Reduce-motion drops rises, slides and
    height changes; a status affordance that carries information is not in that category. That is
    also why this is a `Style.Animations` loop rather than a transition: there is no property change
    to interpolate, so it has no Full/Reduced pair and no MotionResourceBinder alias.
  -->
  <Style Selector="controls|Icon.spinner">
    <Setter Property="Data" Value="{DynamicResource IconScanning}" />
    <Setter Property="Size" Value="{DynamicResource SpinnerSize}" />
    <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="{DynamicResource SpinnerStrokeThickness}" />
    <Setter Property="SourceBox" Value="0,0,14,14" />
    <Setter Property="RenderTransformOrigin" Value="50%,50%" />
    <Style.Animations>
      <Animation Duration="0:0:1.1" IterationCount="Infinite" Easing="LinearEasing">
        <KeyFrame Cue="0%">
          <Setter Property="RotateTransform.Angle" Value="0.0" />
        </KeyFrame>
        <KeyFrame Cue="100%">
          <Setter Property="RotateTransform.Angle" Value="360.0" />
        </KeyFrame>
      </Animation>
    </Style.Animations>
  </Style>
</Styles>
